A||||6||dman||Convertible weather||||6||
Z||000000||dman||12-29-2000||04:27 PM||||Hello everyone. I will admit it. I'm spoiled. The weather here in Southern California is awesome. Its like 78 degrees outside. Clear, bright and sunny. So nice in fact that I drove one of my project cars to Arizona this past Xmas weekend. It is a convertible that I'm restoring.<P>I removed the original top (didn't like it) and I've yet to design a new top. So I drove it approximately 300 miles with no top. It was awesome!!! The first real ride I've taken in this car since working on the mechanicals (major tuneup, new grandam brakes, new tcc solenoid, trannie filter, water pump, all new hoses, yada yada yada).<P>I'll be storing this fiero in AZ for a few months so I can free up some room in my garage for my other projects.<P>Perhaps next year I'll find the time to write up an article on it. It would be nice to see more convertible fieros on the road.<P><BR>&lt;IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=840623&a=6111033&p=36510745"&gt;<P>Hmmm...couldn't get it to show. Oh well. Click here to see the car.<BR> <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=840623&a=6111033&p=36510745" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=840623&a=6111033&p=36510745</A> <P><p>[This message has been edited by dman (edited 12-29-2000).]||||reg||6
